# CR4. EXISTS r.B subseteq A -- existential in SUBCLASS position.
# This is the direction a one-sided normalization loses; see hazards/polarity.ttl.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :r a owl:ObjectProperty .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] rdfs:subClassOf :A .
